From: thrivetoday <289389247+thrivetoday@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:36:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] DualSense support: native HID input, rumble from game
 events, R2 as fire and per-weapon adaptive triggers

A Bluetooth DualSense that Steam or a remapper has switched to its extended report (0x31) gave no input through
Windows.Gaming.Input, and the engine read only the first gamepad, so remappers' virtual pads were ignored too.

- crate::dualsense reads DualSense / DualSense Edge pads from their HID reports (USB 0x01, Bluetooth 0x01 / 0x31)
  and writes the rumble motors and the right trigger's effect (Bluetooth CRC-32, padded to the longest output report).
- input_map::Pads merges every pad; Port Options' "Fire button: R2" reads R2's travel as fire at the held weapon's
  fire point (R1 still crouches).
- crate::haptics: short pulses from wrench hits, damage, shots, landings and camera shakes; R2's per-weapon feel
  synced to the game's firing (the R.Y.N.O.'s salvo, the Blaster's shots); Port Options rows Vibration, Vibration
  strength, Fire button and Trigger effects in both menus.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
