From: thrivetoday <289389247+thrivetoday@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 02:19:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Gadgetron Movement System: Port Options "Controller" page
 listing the controllers, a controller lock, and a Veldin HelpDesk note

Idea by roxas997 on the ReRAC Discord: the controllers under the game's own lore name.

- Port Options' Controller row (value "GMS") opens the Gadgetron Movement System page: every connected device (keyboard
  and mouse, the DualSense, Bevy's gamepads by name) as Active (last used) / Available; X locks the game to one device
  (Locked / Off) or frees it. Both the pause menu's and the main menu's Port Options.
- On Veldin the help box shows a text-only note about the GMS once (help::Help::request_port: no help record).
- RC_GMS_TRACE=1 traces the note's conditions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
