From da69e7c8ef48b8b09d547d030eddc1b87db1365d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thrivetoday <289389247+thrivetoday@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:55:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] Controller page holds the controller settings; port pages
 keep their frames and, in the pause menu, centre the title and stretch the
 list

- Port Options ends with a "Controller" page button (no value); Vibration, Vibration strength, Fire button and Trigger
  effects move to the Controller (Gadgetron Movement System) page, above the connected controllers.
- Between two pages of the same frames the frames hold (frame::FrameMobys::hold): backing out of the Controller page
  played them back to the frames' parent layout, the main menu's small Options panel.
- Pause-menu port pages: frame::PanelAdjust moves the corner joints (rects and the engine's 3D frames) to centre the
  title panel and stretch the list from under the title to the hints; port::VISIBLE 4 -> 7. The game's pages are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
