From 896bd630972708928f65b08ee4ebcf6dfa0e87c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thrivetoday <289389247+thrivetoday@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 20:06:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] DualSense 1.1.1: focus, GMS note per new game and in the
 Help Log, Lightbar setting

Fixes from the ReRAC Discord's testing:
- Pads are read, and rumble and R2's effect sent, only while the game's window has
  the focus: the DualSense's own HID reports arrived regardless, unlike
  Windows.Gaming.Input's (input_map::Pads::focused, haptics_frame).
- The Gadgetron Movement System note shows in every new game's Veldin (level 0
  loaded with under 5 minutes played), not once ever; a reload after a death does
  not show it again (gms::Gms::shown_at). Once seen, the Help Log lists it last
  (PageMenu::gms_in_log), outside the saved log, so saves stay the game's.
  MenuAssets::msg_in resolves port text ids first, also with the Help Log's
  all_text swap.
- Controller page row Lightbar: Default (nothing sent) / Off / Orange / Green /
  Blue / Health (green to red with Ratchet's health over max_hp), key lightbar;
  dualsense sends valid flag 1 0x04 and, once, the lightbar setup.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
